{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_api_layered_request_flow", "label": "Layered Request Flow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L3-L29", "rationale": "Component \u2192 Feature Hook \u2192 API Service \u2192 Supabase \u2192 PostgreSQL. Every request takes the same path so the Supabase surface stays in one replaceable layer and the UI never couples to the database client.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_ui_layer", "label": "UI Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L35-L49", "rationale": "Responsible for rendering only. May call hooks, must never import Supabase. Named examples: TodoCard, Column, BoardHeader.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_hooks_layer", "label": "Hooks Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L53-L66", "rationale": "Owns business logic and orchestrates React Query, optimistic updates, cache updates, loading state and errors. Hooks must never contain SQL \u2014 that keeps the query layer swappable.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_api_layer", "label": "API Service Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L69-L88", "rationale": "Pure Supabase calls only, one file per feature (boardsApi.ts, todosApi.ts, columnsApi.ts, membersApi.ts). Isolating database communication here is what makes the 'component imports Supabase means the architecture is broken' rule checkable.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_database_layer", "label": "Database Layer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L91-L96", "rationale": "The final layer; only API files communicate with it.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_query_keys", "label": "Predictable Query Keys", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L137-L163", "rationale": "Every feature owns its keys and they follow a fixed shape \u2014 [\"boards\"], [\"board\", boardId], [\"columns\", boardId], [\"todos\", boardId], [\"members\", boardId], [\"comments\", todoId], [\"labels\", boardId]. Random keys are banned because cache patching depends on knowing the exact key from anywhere in the app.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_mutation_lifecycle", "label": "Standard Mutation Lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L167-L193", "rationale": "onMutate \u2192 optimistic update \u2192 mutation \u2192 rollback on error \u2192 final cache sync. One lifecycle for every mutation means rollback behaviour is never re-invented per feature.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_optimistic_updates", "label": "Required Optimistic Updates", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L197-L217", "rationale": "Mandatory for create/delete/move/rename todo, create column, reorder columns and assign user. Realtime is explicitly planned to reuse the same cache-update functions, which is why the patch logic must live outside the mutation closures.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_error_handling", "label": "Mutation Error Contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L219-L230", "rationale": "Every mutation returns typed errors, rolls back its optimistic update and shows user feedback. Unexpected errors must never fail silently.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_pagination", "label": "Cursor Pagination Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L233-L240", "rationale": "Avoided until necessary; when needed, cursor pagination is preferred over offset because board rows reorder constantly and offsets would skip or duplicate cards.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_filtering_in_hooks", "label": "Filtering Belongs In Hooks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L243-L265", "rationale": "useFilteredTodos() composes on top of useTodos() rather than filtering inside a component, so a filter is shared and testable instead of duplicated per render tree.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_realtime_cache_update", "label": "Realtime Updates Caches", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L269-L291", "rationale": "Supabase Realtime \u2192 Event \u2192 Update Cache \u2192 React Re-render. Never refetch the whole board on an event.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_naming_conventions", "label": "API And Hook Naming Conventions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L295-L341", "rationale": "getX/createX/updateX/deleteX for API functions and useX/useCreateX/useDeleteX for hooks, so the layer a symbol belongs to is readable from its name alone.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_typed_return_types", "label": "Typed API Return Types", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L345-L361", "rationale": "Every API function returns a typed object (Promise<Board>, Promise<Todo[]>, Promise<Member[]>); any and unknown are banned so type drift surfaces at the compiler rather than at runtime.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_validation_policy", "label": "Two-Sided Validation Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L365-L391", "rationale": "Validation runs before the API call (trim, required fields, length, date, email) for UX, and again in the database for correctness. Frontend validation alone is never trusted.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_supabase_import_rule", "label": "Only API Files May Import Supabase", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L395-L401", "rationale": "The rule of thumb that makes the layering falsifiable: if a component imports Supabase directly, the architecture is broken.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_api_layered_request_flow", "target": "docs_api_ui_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L11-L29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_layered_request_flow", "target": "docs_api_hooks_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L11-L29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_layered_request_flow", "target": "docs_api_api_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L11-L29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_layered_request_flow", "target": "docs_api_database_layer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "L11-L29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_supabase_import_rule", "target": "docs_api_layered_request_flow", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/API.md", "source_location": "